{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1oQYHyyad3mhgUwB4wc", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I've stopped testing because the device connection failed partway through, and I couldn't restore the settings I changed. I did not sign off.\n\n**Bugs filed (developer replies):**\n1. **Timebox minutes, 0 not saved** (not_persisted). With Timebox on, I typed 0 in the minutes field. The \"-\" button disabled, but the Scheduling row kept \"3 mins\" after leaving. The developer could not reproduce it.\n2. **Timebox minutes overwritten after off/on** (wrong_value, plus a follow-up on the stored value). I set 7 minutes, turned Timebox off, left the screen, reopened it, and turned it back on. The field showed 20 and the Scheduling row kept \"20 mins\" after leaving and reopening. I reproduced it twice (with 3, then with 7). The developer could not reproduce it either. A 45-minute test passed only because the screen was not reopened while Timebox was off.\n\n**Checked and looked correct:**\n- **Timebox:** a changed value persists after leaving the screen, and turning Timebox off hides the field.\n- **Theme change:** Night and Day applied immediately to open screens and to the home screen. Cancel in the theme dialog kept the current theme.\n- **Answer-button intervals:** labels matched the saved due dates (comer Easy 5d, due 2026-11-18; mesa Easy 3d, due 2026-11-16). \"Show button time\" off hid the labels, and labels survived device rotation.\n- **Browser subtitle:** \"Spanish | 4 cards shown\", \"All decks | 7 cards shown\", and \"French | 3 cards shown\" matched the list after deck changes, search and collapse. Rotation with the search open kept the subtitle correct.\n\n**Left in a changed state (device disconnected before restoring):**\n- Timebox is on with 20 minutes. It was originally Disabled.\n- Theme is Day. It was originally Follow system.\n- \"Show button time\" is on, as it was originally.\n- Cards \"comer\" and \"mesa\" were answered Easy during testing.\n\nThe device tool started returning BrokenPipeError on every call after the browser checks. Once the device is reconnected, the Timebox and Theme settings need restoring to their original values."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 159, "cache_read_input_tokens": 203026, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 159}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ccc65579-67bb-4307-bd03-8c1448683909", "uuid": "98b607e3-6b75-49fd-95b0-e7fbf51c4633", "timestamp": "2026-11-13T23:32:58.991Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1oQY37D8ShpLNsWDW2N"}
